{
  "_comment": [
    "TEMPLATE — not the live manifest. Run `even-hub init` in a TEMP directory",
    "(it scaffolds a whole project and would clobber src/), then copy its",
    "generated app.json here and merge these fields in.",
    "",
    "The CLI owns the canonical schema. Field names below reflect the SDK docs;",
    "if the generated manifest disagrees, the generated one is right — fix this",
    "template rather than fighting the CLI.",
    "",
    "Strip every _comment key before shipping."
  ],

  "name": "JOAT",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "description": "Voice to HUD, relayed to the Mac brain.",

  "_comment_websocket": [
    "THE ONE THAT SILENTLY BREAKS EVERYTHING.",
    "Exact-match domains only — no wildcards, no bare IPs that churn with DHCP.",
    "The Hub blocks unlisted domains with no error the plugin can see: the",
    "socket simply never opens, which looks identical to a Mac that is offline.",
    "",
    "Use a stable hostname. Tailscale MagicDNS is the least fragile:",
    "  wss://mac-studio.tailnet-name.ts.net:8787",
    "A .local mDNS name works on one LAN but not across networks.",
    "",
    "Keep this in sync with VITE_MAC_WS_URL in .env — if they disagree, the",
    "plugin dials a domain the manifest never allowed."
  ],
  "websocketDomains": [
    "wss://mac-studio.your-tailnet.ts.net:8787"
  ],

  "_comment_permissions": [
    "microphone — glasses mic via audioControl. Required for Phase 0.",
    "location   — only if you use getAppLocation; drop it until you do.",
    "camera     — phone camera for the vision path (Phase 4). Drop until then.",
    "album      — photo picker. Drop until used.",
    "",
    "Request nothing you do not use yet: every extra permission is another",
    "prompt the wearer must accept, and another review question at submission."
  ],
  "permissions": ["microphone"],

  "_comment_entry": "Vite build output. Confirm against the generated manifest.",
  "entry": "dist/index.html"
}
